<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Edmund Andros</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1637">1637</a>–<a href="/years/1714">1714</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Sir Edmund Andros</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Edmund Andros was an English colonial administrator who governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> from 1674 to 1681. In 1686 he became governor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominion">Dominion</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-england">New England</a>, which merged the northern colonies under royal rule without elected assemblies. His rule was deeply resented, and after news of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glorious-revolution">Glorious Revolution</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a> rose and deposed him in 1689. He later governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/edmund-andros.jpg" alt="Edmund Andros" width="320" height="387" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mary Beale · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sir_Edmund_Andros_by_Beale.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
